Idea: attempt 6 with a different placement of the plaintext constants. I merge `c0` and `−c4` into the low-level linear part (`z·c1 − 3e`), where they are added before the last multiplication. The final result is then just w·g plus that sum. The operation counts stay the same, but the order of the adds changes how CHEHAB aligns levels.

